<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android's own backup, for devices on API 30 and below.

    The whole of the app's file storage is included, not just the save file. That distinction is
    the entire point: when training was lost it was the save file itself that went bad, and a
    backup that faithfully restores a bad save file has restored nothing. Including the directory
    carries the spare copy (winter-arc.json.bak) and every dated snapshot with it, so a restored
    phone arrives with the same means of recovery the original had.

    Shared preferences are deliberately left out. They hold the cloud sign-in tokens, which should
    not travel, and the backup folder's permission grant, which cannot. Restoring it would show
    a folder that looks chosen but can no longer be written to.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="file" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
